#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384638 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "80c443e5-a0b2-5aae-ac8d-27449a8049a3" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of a Plane Given Its Cartesian Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2346d3ff-5938-5252-b9cd-952c41afb699" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384640} {:answer/id #uuid "89228a02-e815-56ab-9fbf-a197e79a148d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384641}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89228a02-e815-56ab-9fbf-a197e79a148d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384641} :answer-field/id #uuid "404719b6-4d8f-5e11-9be9-036bda1402f6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384639} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c388a551-0e74-54e5-9839-9cca156461dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384643}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c388a551-0e74-54e5-9839-9cca156461dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384643} :answer-field/id #uuid "565e5b01-c043-5165-b017-b140005d6c7b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384642} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "523b3861-685d-571c-988d-ea0188229f52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384645}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "523b3861-685d-571c-988d-ea0188229f52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384645} :answer-field/id #uuid "206cc8c3-2056-520b-a460-0d49602ce8e2" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384644}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "925e27d5-9a24-540e-b569-c14fe85a8802" :question/math-academy-id "q-326901" :question/problem "Given the Cartesian equation $2x-y+2z+6=0$ of the plane $Π$, find an equation of $Π$ in the form $(r-p)\\cdot n=0.$\n\n$(r-⟨0,0,$ \n{{field-1}}\n$⟩)\\cdot ⟨2,$\n{{field-2}}\n, \n{{field-3}}\n$⟩=0$" :question/worked-solution "First, from the equation of the plane we get that the normal vector of $Π$ is $n=⟨2,-1,2⟩.$\n\nNow, we solve the Cartesian equation of $Π$ for $z$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-y+2z+6 & =0 \\\\ z & =-x+\\frac{y}{2}-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we put $x=0$ and $y=0$, we get $z=-3.$ Hence, the point $P(0,0,-3)$ lies on $Π.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,0,-3⟩.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-⟨0,0,-3⟩)\\cdot ⟨2,-1,2⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384646 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0efe5b11-2c87-58e9-bf7c-e1eecb07adf2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Cartesian Equation of the Plane Parallel To Two Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55723dcb-605f-595d-8fae-1ee5436e7a81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15x-8y-3z-67=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384648} {:answer/id #uuid "42a8ae72-16c3-587a-a3e7-b75bffe928ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-5y+z-70=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384649} {:answer/id #uuid "803a1755-2134-5aa8-a86a-8015bacc22d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x+y-67=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384650} {:answer/id #uuid "2bd5cb89-4f60-5887-afe3-a7c5a3523298" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15x-8y-3z+70=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384651} {:answer/id #uuid "31dcdae4-9b1f-53d5-a9d2-7fbe89fc944a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x-2y+3z=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384652}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55723dcb-605f-595d-8fae-1ee5436e7a81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15x-8y-3z-67=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384648} :answer-field/id #uuid "362de8bd-fdfa-5aa6-b00e-5111d888298e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384647}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c5938084-81eb-59aa-b8c4-275f8497be94" :question/math-academy-id "q-33142" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the points $A(2,-5,1)$, $P(4,-2,3)$ and $Q(5,1,0).$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A,P$ and $Q$ are $a=⟨2,-5,1⟩,\\,p=⟨4,-2,3⟩,$ and $q=⟨5,1,0⟩.$\n\nFirst, using the $3$ points we build $2$ vectors parallel to the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1} & =\\overset{\\to }{AP} \\\\  & =⟨4,-2,3⟩-⟨2,-5,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,3,2⟩ \\\\ {v}_{2} & =\\overset{\\to }{AQ} \\\\  & =⟨5,1,0⟩-⟨2,-5,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,6,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow,  we need to find the normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={v}_{1}\\times {v}_{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 6 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-15i+8j+3k \\\\  & =⟨-15,8,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-15,8,3⟩ & =⟨4,-2,3⟩\\cdot ⟨-15,8,3⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-15,8,3⟩ & =-67\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-15,8,3⟩ & =-67 \\\\ -15x+8y+3z & =-67 \\\\ -15x+8y+3z+67 & =0 \\\\ 15x-8y-3z-67 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384653 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2173739c-cd59-58ed-a265-8ee88c982ae0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Cartesian Equation of the Plane Perpendicular To a Given Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7fde512d-6ec1-5523-9f7e-f1e5a94c1668" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384655}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7fde512d-6ec1-5523-9f7e-f1e5a94c1668" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384655} :answer-field/id #uuid "f08ab864-495e-565c-a51c-18ba0a886950" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384654} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec6f1fa2-0c28-5b15-b0e2-c385a4c95fc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384657}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec6f1fa2-0c28-5b15-b0e2-c385a4c95fc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384657} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d8b4801-7443-5015-9570-7463ee433851" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384656} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85277b5a-1a68-5e4c-b1e5-9d1d322b6907" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384659}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85277b5a-1a68-5e4c-b1e5-9d1d322b6907" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384659} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdd60602-2771-5921-8d18-9737745e767b" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384658}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2c496c1b-87a2-58b0-9bd2-be54b651106d" :question/math-academy-id "q-336110" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(1,-2,5)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n${\\begin{aligned}x=4+3t \\\\ y=1-4t \\\\ z=-3-2t\\end{aligned}.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$x\\,-4y\\,-\\,$ \n{{field-2}} $z\\,-$\n{{field-3}}$\\,=0$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨1,-2,5⟩.$ From the parametrical equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨3,-4,-2⟩.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨3,-4,-2⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-4,-2⟩ & =⟨1,-2,5⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-4,-2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-4,-2⟩ & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-4,-2⟩ & =1 \\\\ 3x-4y-2z & =1 \\\\ 3x-4y-2z-1 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384660 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2173739c-cd59-58ed-a265-8ee88c982ae0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Cartesian Equation of the Plane Perpendicular To a Given Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95b444a5-a882-5dae-925b-0761a2f35516" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384662} {:answer/id #uuid "6240e868-9f25-5939-963b-606c431c6371" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384663}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6240e868-9f25-5939-963b-606c431c6371" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384663} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab8b83ee-829c-5df6-be8e-efc7065c5235" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384661} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b77db0e-1095-5326-a14f-940620890dd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384665}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b77db0e-1095-5326-a14f-940620890dd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384665} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e08e4b4-8eb5-5c61-9db3-3ce32c341c1d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384664} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe6d6055-d025-5fa0-82c0-ee849150e945" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384667}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe6d6055-d025-5fa0-82c0-ee849150e945" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384667} :answer-field/id #uuid "104d5e11-5ced-57b0-9d21-836ffcb70d45" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384666}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "db29741f-b982-55e1-b925-152441611363" :question/math-academy-id "q-336201" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(-2,3,1)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n$r=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n$3x\\,-\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n$y\\,+\\,$\n{{field-2}}\n$z\\,+$\n{{field-3}}\n\n$=0$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨-2,3,1⟩.$  From the vectorial equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨3,-5,2⟩.$  So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨3,-5,2⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-5,2⟩ & =⟨-2,3,1⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-5,2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-5,2⟩ & =-19\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-5,2⟩ & =-19 \\\\ 3x-5y+2z & =-19 \\\\ 3x-5y+2z+19 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384668 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "80c443e5-a0b2-5aae-ac8d-27449a8049a3" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of a Plane Given Its Cartesian Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d0eb7ad-9b50-5dc6-8b87-7f76312128ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384670}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d0eb7ad-9b50-5dc6-8b87-7f76312128ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384670} :answer-field/id #uuid "b27f8f14-201a-514c-be9b-ed56526f88d6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384669} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e32d4500-7940-5053-86bb-fbf9704e32fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384672}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e32d4500-7940-5053-86bb-fbf9704e32fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384672} :answer-field/id #uuid "40f9f4ed-dcee-5879-891b-4aeea776472c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384671} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c8a3a99-7496-5337-b5d9-580ecd2bdac2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384674}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c8a3a99-7496-5337-b5d9-580ecd2bdac2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384674} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7ce9af2-3886-50d4-8ccd-8959a18d4900" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384673}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e72d0f67-c2b4-5692-91cc-01e26d063987" :question/math-academy-id "q-336228" :question/problem "Given the Cartesian equation $5x+2y+z-4=0$ of the plane $Π$, find an equation of $Π$ in the form $(r-p)\\cdot n=0.$\n\n$(r-⟨0,0,$\n{{field-1}}\n$⟩)\\cdot ⟨$\n{{field-2}} $,\\,2\\,,$\n{{field-3}}\n$⟩=0$" :question/worked-solution "First, from the equation of the plane we get that the normal vector of $Π$ is $n=⟨5,2,1⟩.$\n\nNow, we solve the Cartesian equation of $Π$ for $z$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+2y+z-4 & =0 \\\\ z & =-5x-2y+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we put $x=0$ and $y=0$, we get $z=4.$ Hence, the point $P(0,0,4)$ lies on $Π.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,0,4⟩.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-⟨0,0,4⟩)\\cdot ⟨5,\\,2\\,,1⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
